{
  "id": "between-groups-design",
  "term": "between-groups design",
  "definition": "A between-groups design is a study setup that compares outcomes across separate groups of participants, such as one group with one condition and another group with a different condition. In this design, the groups are contrasted with each other on the same measures rather than tracking changes within a single group.",
